			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decompose EchoAction RPC module into file-per-struct submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `Source/RPC/EchoAction` module to align with the project-wide PascalCase file-per-struct convention. Extract core logic into dedicated `EchoActionServer.rs`, `ExtensionHostRegistry.rs`, `ExtensionRouter.rs`, and `ResolveMethodPriority.rs` files.\n\nThe `Struct` in `EchoActionServer` encapsulates the singleton submission gate and task dispatch logic, coordinating with the `Echo` scheduler and priority lanes. `ExtensionHostRegistry` manages the mapping of extension identifiers to active host processes, while `ExtensionRouter` provides lookup capabilities for routing requests. `ResolveMethodPriority` defines the static mapping logic for assigning Echo priority lanes (High, Normal, Low) based on incoming wire method names.\n\nAll files adhere to the `Struct` and `Fn` naming patterns required by Tauri's `generate_handler!` macro for correct symbol resolution, continuing the architectural consistency established in recent `Workspace`, `Telemetry`, and `Vine` refactors.",
			"SHA": "74aa2e6a8f907db173a00a6b9f858f81c536b5b3"
